#AUTO 103
#NEEDED 0
# DE-SELECTED: this is a deliberate whole-disk action, not a routine health
# check — a full 29 GiB sector-for-sector copy that takes many minutes.
# Trigger it on purpose (its own run) when you actually want a full image;
# the routine sweep should never grind through 29 GiB. Kept in the image so
# the roster shows it was deliberately skipped, not missing.
# Full linear eMMC -> SD dump (issue 110m) — the plain, simple version:
# copy the WHOLE eMMC to the SD's dump region, sector for sector, no map.
# eMMC sector N lands at SD sector 0x800000 + N, so getting the image back
# is just "read that region back and concatenate" — nothing to reconstruct,
# nothing that can tear in the log. Moves all 29 GiB (zeros included), so
# it is slower than a sparse dump but dead simple and idempotent (safe to
# re-run / resume after a power cut).
#
# emmc_dump_to_sd (in src/012-emmc.c) reads chunk by chunk via ADMA2 at
# HS200 and writes each with the multi-block IDMAC writer. Bottom LED is the
# progress bar; "[dump] at <lba>" prints ~every 256 MB; the final
# "[dump] complete total=.. packed=.." line (packed=total) tells the pull
# side to read the whole region.
#
# NOTE the 29 GiB does not fit a 28.9 GiB FAT32 USB drive raw — pull it
# compressed (dd | gzip), which collapses the ~22 GiB of zeros to almost
# nothing. Writes only the SD dump region (from 0x800000), never the eMMC.

CALL sd_init
CALL sd_speed
CALL emmc_init
CALL emmc_hs200
CALL emmc_dump
